{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgyx6g3N5bo9aL5mh1upH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. I think nothing is left that I must do. The journal showed no active objective after I reported to Never-Sold. If the game continues, it would probably be through Never-Sold or the Tsaxi household: whoever I chose, or the two prisoners left behind. I'd check back with Never-Sold and Tsaxi to see if anything new opens.\n\n2. Nominally Never-Sold, who runs the Chainbreakers' house. She sent me to Rows-For-Another, and I reported back to her after the Tsaxi job. I work for her because she gave me the work and the coin, and her house is the one that frees people from Owings. I wasn't formally hired, though. I picked up errands from her, and nothing in the journal or dialogue said I had a standing role.\n\n3. Two things. The journal was empty at the start of the new work, so I had no written objective and had to guess where to go. The Tsaxi menu also showed the persuade option twice, and I wasn't sure whether the two entries did different things. I also wasn't sure how the Owing system worked, in particular what happens to the two prisoners I didn't choose.\n\n4. The three-way choice worked because each prisoner gave one clear reason. The story moved naturally from the Rows-For-Another buy-out into the next job. I'd fix three things:\n   - Add journal entries when a quest begins, so a player isn't left with a blank journal.\n   - Remove the duplicated persuade option.\n   - Show some consequence for the two prisoners I left held, since that was the part that stayed with me. Right now the choice ends without any aftermath."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2713,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2713},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"stan